    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d514">

                <pb facs="0623" n="1457" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/337</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-11T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1100. Your No. 2284, April 10, 1 p.m. You are authorized to inform the Foreign
                    Office and if you see fit announce publicly that the two Netherlands steamers,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Java</hi> now at Savannah and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Juno</hi> now at Curaçao, or other shipping under Dutch
                    control of approximately the same tonnage which the Netherlands Government may
                    designate, may at once load grain at a United States Gulf port and proceed to
                    the Netherlands, it being understood that ships aggregating approximately the
                    same tonnage will leave the Netherlands for a North American port simultaneously
                    with the departure of these vessels from the United States for the
                    Netherlands.</p>
                <p>We estimate that these two vessels together with the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hollandia</hi> will permit of the immediate lifting for the Netherlands of
                    approximately 14,000 tons of bread cereals which, of course, will be credited on
                    account of the 100,000 tons of bread cereals offered to be placed at the
                    disposal of the Netherlands Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
